    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nTwo files touched, keeping structural impact minimal:\n\n1. **New function class** `RejectDisposableEmail.java` \u2014 a small, cohesive unit (one method, WMC_other = 0, no surrounding class complexity to hold). It reads the already-normalized email, extracts the domain, and throws when it's on the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step in right after `normalizeEmail`, so the email is syntactically valid and lower-cased before the domain check runs.\n\n## Key decisions\n\n- **Reused the existing `MissingFieldsException`** (which its handler maps to **400**) rather than defining a new exception + handler + escalation YAML. That avoids touching 3 extra files, and the check naturally slots into the existing email-processing chain.\n- **No existing method or class grew** \u2014 the behaviour lives entirely in a new, isolated function, following the project's `Validate/Ensure/Reject` one-step-per-function convention.\n- Absent/blank emails pass through unchanged, preserving backward compatibility with the \"fully unique owner accepted by every rule\" baseline.\n\nThe new acceptance test `errorRejectsDisposableDomain` (POST with `x@mailinator.com` \u2192 400) passes, and all pre-existing tests remain green.",
